<GuideLayout 
  title="Sustainable Activewear: Sourcing GRS-Certified Fabrics"
  description="How to leverage recycled materials to build a high-premium, eco-conscious fitness brand that resonates with modern consumers."
  publishDate="June 26, 2026"
>
  <p>Sustainability is no longer a niche market—it's the core of the premium activewear sector. Consumers are demanding transparency, and GRS (Global Recycled Standard) certification is the gold standard for verifying recycled content in textiles.</p>

  <h2>Why GRS Matters for Your Brand</h2>
  <p>The GRS certification doesn't just track recycled materials; it also enforces social and environmental requirements and chemical restrictions. By sourcing GRS-certified recycled nylon and polyester from Fitclo, your brand can legitimately claim a lower carbon footprint and higher ethical standards.</p>

  <h2>Performance Without Compromise</h2>
  <p>A common misconception is that recycled fabrics are less durable. Our latest R&D has proven that recycled Nylon 6,6 offers the exact same tensile strength, moisture-wicking properties, and 4-way stretch as virgin nylon, ensuring your sustainable line performs at an elite level.</p>

